Orphan is a 2009 psychological slasher film directed by Jaume Collet-Serra
and written by David Leslie Johnson from a story by Alex Mace.

11
00:55:55,000 --> 00:56:01,000
The film stars Vera Farmiga, Peter Sarsgaard, Isabelle
Fuhrman, CCH Pounder, and Jimmy Bennett.

12
01:01:00,000 --> 01:01:06,000
The plot centers on a couple who, after the death of their unborn child,
adopt a psychopathic nine-year-old girl with a mysterious past.

13
01:06:05,000 --> 01:06:11,000
The film is an international co-production between the
United States, Canada, Germany and France.

14
01:11:10,000 --> 01:11:16,000
It was produced by Joel Silver and Susan Downey of Dark Castle Entertainment, and
Leonardo DiCaprio and Jennifer Davisson Killoran of Appian Way Productions.

15
01:16:15,000 --> 01:16:21,000
Principal photography for the film took place in Canada, in the cities of St.

16
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:26,000
Thomas, Toronto, Port Hope, and Montreal.

17
01:26:25,000 --> 01:26:31,000
Orphan was released by Warner Bros.

18
01:31:30,000 --> 01:31:36,000
Pictures in the United States and Canada on July 24, 2009.

19
01:36:35,000 --> 01:36:41,000
It was released in Germany on October 22, and in France on December 30.

20
01:41:40,000 --> 01:41:46,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and
grossed $78.8 million worldwide.

21
01:46:45,000 --> 01:46:51,000
The film successfully launched its titular film series starring Fuhrman, including a prequel
titled Orphan: First Kill (2022), and its sequel titled Orphans in production.

